# rBrowser packages for apt and dnf

The signed apt and dnf repositories of [rBrowser](https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@), a development
browser that shows every breakpoint of a site at once, for x86-64. Served at <@BASE_URL@>.

Debian and Ubuntu:

```bash
sudo install -d -m 0755 /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL @BASE_URL@/rbrowser-packages.asc | sudo tee /etc/apt/keyrings/rbrowser-packages.asc > /dev/null
curl -fsSL @BASE_URL@/rbrowser.sources | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/rbrowser.sources > /dev/null
sudo apt update
sudo apt install rbrowser
```

Fedora:

```bash
sudo curl -fsSL -o /etc/yum.repos.d/rbrowser.repo @BASE_URL@/rbrowser.repo
sudo dnf install rbrowser
```

`apt upgrade` and `dnf upgrade` then install every new release; rBrowser installed this way does
not replace itself. The repository indexes and the rpm packages are signed with the key
`@FINGERPRINT@`; compare it with the fingerprint dnf shows on the first install, or with
`gpg --show-keys /etc/apt/keyrings/rbrowser-packages.asc`. The last @KEEP@ versions of each
package stay here for a downgrade (`apt install rbrowser=<version>`, `dnf downgrade rbrowser`).

The files are written by the release workflow of
[@REPOSITORY@](https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@) with every release - issues and changes go
there, not here. The handbook's installation page:
<https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@/wiki/installation>.
